id: glass
name: Glass
kind: battlefield
envQuality: true
hardnessShift: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A sheet of glass over the ground, one Hardness Rank harder than what is under it.
text: >
  Glass: This Square is encased in glass, increasing its Hardness Rank by 1. If this
  Environmental Quality is applied through an effect, remove all other Environmental
  Qualities on this Feature.

---

# The same Quality a Feature can have, word for word, and it does the same thing to a Square
# that it does to a Feature: one Rank harder.
#
# `hardnessShift: 1`, added to the ground's Hardness Rank wherever that Rank is read - the
# row on the tab, and the Ground Collision in the window. Held inside the Ranks that exist,
# so glass over Katchin is still Rank 5 rather than a sixth Rank nobody wrote.
#
# --- What is not built ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# "If this Environmental Quality is applied through an effect, remove all other
# Environmental Qualities on this Feature."
#
# Through an effect. No effect in this system applies an Environmental Quality - the ARC
# does, and the player ticks it - so the clause has nothing to fire on. When an effect that
# applies one arrives, this is the rule it has to carry.
#
# Until then the exclusivity is the table's, and ticking Glass beside Metallic is a thing
# the sheet will let you do. It says so rather than refusing quietly.
